TIP:  There is an easy little voicing surrounding the (D) which appears in the intro and again after the chorus (although only chords are shown in the chorus).  It's done in three parts:  (1) Strum (D).  (2) Still holding (D) pick the 2nd string, lift off the 1st string and pick it, cover the 1st string and strum (D).  (3) Pick the 1st string, lift off the 1st string and pick it, pick the 2nd string, strum (D).  Begin song.  (Notes may or may not transpose.)  After the chorus (denoted by (D) (D)) you play the same thing followed by (D) (A) (D) as in "kick off your shoes . . ."

TIP:  Not too fast.
  

